# Bench capture: section 8 reproduction attempt (laptop-as-fake-dongle), 2026-09-28 laptop side.
# Fake dongle: tools/bt-obd/obd-ble-sim.py --mode idle --rpm 2400 --coolant 90 --intake 42 --speed 55
# Slave board COM8 (esp32s3-rgb-slave-obdtest), reset right after the simulator started.
# Verdict: section 8 FAILED -- the board never connected to the fake dongle.
#
# TWO independent findings (both block section 8 as written):
#  A) The simulator's OWN self-test says the board cannot find it:
#       advertising service 0000fff0-...  status=2
#       --- advertisement seen by a PASSIVE scanner (rssi=-87 addr=7DEC7BC78A99 type=0) ---
#         service uuids : ['42594420-4155-544f-e0a9-e50e24dcca9e']
#         VERDICT       : FFF0 NOT in the advertisement -> board would never find us
#     Windows puts the service UUID in the SCAN RESPONSE, while the firmware scans PASSIVELY
#     (ObdTransportBle: scan_->setActiveScan(false) and it filters on isAdvertisingService(FFF0)).
#  B) --mode idle NEVER answers AT commands (it only notifies unsolicited), so it can never
#     produce the section 8 expected line `SRC speed=link rpm=obd coolant=obd intake=obd |
#     ...2400rpm 90.0C 42.0C...`. Simulator log: cmd=0 notify=0 write=0 for the whole run.
#
# Simulator side log (66 s, verbatim):
#   advertising service 0000fff0-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb  status=2
#   t=  5.1s subs=0 cmd=0 notify=0 write=0 err=0 | rpm=2400 cool=90 speed=55 intake=42
#   ... (subs/cmd/notify/write stay 0 for every sample) ...
#   t= 66.0s subs=0 cmd=0 notify=0 write=0 err=0 | rpm=2400 cool=90 speed=55 intake=42
#   stopped: cmd=0 notify=0 write=0 err=0
